Two-Headed Giant (Commander Duels v0.5.0 spike): the computer player knows its teammate.

Reason: XMage's AI keeps only itself out of the targets it searches for a harmful spell, and sorts
the targets it picks outside a search into its own and everyone else's, so with teams it aimed burn
at its teammate (seen in Commander Duels' four-bot games: the search cannot tell the targets apart
while the spell is still on the stack). Its position score also counted only its own permanents and
one opponent's. With this, in a team game (Game.getTeammates, from part 1) the teammate is kept out
of harmful single targets in the search, a teammate and the teammate's objects count as the AI's own
side when it picks targets, and each side's permanents are the whole team's. Other games are
unchanged.
Needs part 1.
Upstream: none yet; to be offered to magefree/mage with parts 1 and 2.
Remove when: XMage upstream's AI supports teams, or Two-Headed Giant is dropped.

